WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.562
Coding Exercise 5 is the most important cardinality exercise in the assignment.

00:00:05.562 --> 00:00:09.152
The required grain is one row per patient.

00:00:09.152 --> 00:00:17.147
You need admission count, lab count, and prescription count, and patients with no activity must still remain.

00:00:17.147 --> 00:00:22.122
Do not directly join all three detail tables and then use COUNT star.

00:00:22.122 --> 00:00:26.057
That creates combinations and can inflate the measures.

00:00:26.057 --> 00:00:32.622
Instead, summarize each child table by patient_id inside the common table expressions.

00:00:32.622 --> 00:00:35.752
Each summary should return one row per patient with one count.

00:00:35.752 --> 00:00:39.752
Then LEFT JOIN those summaries to the patient table.

00:00:39.752 --> 00:00:46.332
Use COALESCE or another missing-value fallback so a patient with no activity shows zero instead of NULL.

00:00:46.332 --> 00:00:50.662
After Run and Check, validate the result.

00:00:50.662 --> 00:00:54.162
The number of output rows should equal the number of patients.

00:00:54.162 --> 00:00:58.822
Check one patient with several activities and one patient with no activity.

00:00:58.822 --> 00:01:06.842
This exercise represents a pattern you will use often in dashboards and reporting systems where multiple

00:01:06.842 --> 00:01:10.880
measures must be combined safely at one target grain.
